reset

## WR-284 ceramic RF window, quarter model.
##
## Adapted from the ACE3P tutorial 's3p/window' example, which splits this into
## step1-Make-window.jou (build the solid, export window.sat) and
## step2-Mesh-window.jou (import it, mesh, set sidesets, export window.gen).
## LUME-ACE3P plays ONE journal per cubit module, so the two are joined here and
## the ACIS round-trip is dropped. The tutorial's meshing half named surfaces by
## ID (the numbering its export/import pair produced); the joined journal gets a
## different numbering, so ports and symmetry planes are selected by position
## instead. Every selector also excludes merged (interior) surfaces so that a
## vacuum/ceramic interface can never land in a boundary sideset.

## --- geometry (was step1-Make-window.jou) ---------------------------------- #

#{w284=72.136 }
#{h284=34.163 }

#{cradius = 45 }
#{wdwt    =  3 }
#{cavl    = 15 }

#{wlengthz = 60}


## ceremic window
brick x {w284} y {h284} z {2*wlengthz}
create cylinder height {2*cavl+wdwt} radius {cradius}
unite all
compress ids
webcut volume 1  with plane zplane offset {0.5*wdwt}
webcut volume 2  with plane zplane offset {-0.5*wdwt}

webcut volume all with plane xplane offset 0
delete volume 6 4 5
webcut volume all with plane yplane offset 0
delete volume 1 2 3
compress ids

## --- mesh (was step2-Mesh-window.jou) ------------------------------------- #

volume all scheme tetmesh

merge tolerance 0.0001
imprint body all
merge body all

volume 1 3 sizing function type skeleton scale 5 time_accuracy_level 2 min_size auto max_size 6 max_gradient 1.2
volume 2   sizing function type skeleton scale 3 time_accuracy_level 2 min_size 1.5 max_size 3 max_gradient 1.2

group 'ms' add surface with Is_merged
ms expand size 2
ms expand interval hard


mesh volume all
smooth vol all
smooth surface all

## Ports are the guide ends at z = -/+ wlengthz; the symmetry planes are x = 0
## (sideset 1, magnetic for TE10) and y = 0 (sideset 2, electric). The quarter
## model may sit on either side of each plane, so test the centroid both ways.
group "port7" add surface with z_coord < {-wlengthz+0.01} and not is_merged
group "port8" add surface with z_coord > { wlengthz-0.01} and not is_merged
group "sym1"  add surface with x_coord > -0.01 and x_coord < 0.01 and not is_merged
group "sym2"  add surface with y_coord > -0.01 and y_coord < 0.01 and not is_merged

group "ss6" add surface all

ss6 subtract ms     from ss6
ss6 subtract sym1   from ss6
ss6 subtract sym2   from ss6
ss6 subtract port7  from ss6
ss6 subtract port8  from ss6


sideset 1 surface in sym1
sideset 2 surface in sym2
sideset 7 surface in port7
sideset 8 surface in port8
sideset 6 surface in ss6

block 1 vol 1 3
block 2 vol 2

block all element type tetra10
transform mesh output scale 0.001

export genesis "window.gen" overwrite
